# SRG-APP-000750-AU-000130  -  CAT II
# The Central Log Server must implement an audit reduction capability that
# supports on-demand audit review and analysis.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000750-AU-000130
group:           V-263559
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-003822
control_rev5:    AU-7

contribution:    Audit reduction in Splunk is the search-time knowledge layer applied over
                 indexed records - field extraction, field aliasing, lookups, macros and
                 data models - all of which are application configuration and all of which
                 are applied when an analyst runs a search on demand.

governs:         macros.conf - Reusable fragments of search language.
governs:         props.conf - How incoming data is recognized, parsed and timestamped.
governs:         transforms.conf - Rules that rewrite or route data as it is processed.

check:           props.conf [<source type>] present
check:           macros.conf [<STANZA_NAME>] definition non_empty
check:           transforms.conf [<unique_transform_stanza_name>] present

external:        Which fields and which events constitute the reduced view an analyst
                 reviews is an organization-defined parameter recorded in the system
                 security plan; the product can express any reduction but cannot supply the
                 organization's definition.
external:        Having an analyst available to invoke the reduction, and the review
                 procedure that follows, are organizational.

citation:        props.conf.spec:80 [<spec>] with <spec> = <sourcetype> | host::<host> |
                 source::<source> | rule::<rulename>, :1085 REPORT-<class>, :1102
                 EXTRACT-<class>, :1265 FIELDALIAS-<class>, :1313 EVAL-<fieldname>, :1329
                 LOOKUP-<class>; macros.conf.spec:24 [<STANZA_NAME>], :52 definition =
                 <string>; transforms.conf.spec:68 [<unique_transform_stanza_name>];
                 datamodels.conf.spec:26 [<datamodel_name>].
finding:         Assessed at the application layer alone: no props.conf stanza binds a
                 search-time knowledge layer to the audit source types in scope, or a macro
                 or transform defined for audit review carries no definition, so the
                 application offers no audit reduction for an analyst to apply on demand.
